WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.320
Safe frying: buns, doughnuts and fish rolls.

2
00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:08.340
This is the video for module 2 of Basic Baking and Snacks Production.

3
00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:19.960
Hot oil burns deeper than boiling water, and an oil fire spreads in seconds. Use a deep, heavy pot on a stable burner, with the handle turned inwards.

4
00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:28.760
Fill it no more than one third to half full. Food added to a full pot makes the oil rise and overflow onto the flame.

5
00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:32.720
Keep a lid that fits the pot within arm's reach.

6
00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:37.170
Keep water, wet cloths and children away from the pot.

7
00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:50.560
Heat the oil gradually and check it with a frying thermometer. Most snacks fry well between about 160 and 180 degrees. If oil smokes, turn the heat down at once.

8
00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:58.210
Never throw water on burning oil. It turns to steam instantly and throws burning oil out of the pot.

9
00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:13.190
Turn off the heat if you safely can, slide a fitting lid or fire blanket over the pot, and leave it covered until cool. Do not carry the pot outside. If the fire spreads, get everyone out and call the fire service.

10
00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:24.430
For a burn, cool it under cool running water for 20 minutes. Get medical help for anything larger than a small coin, or on the face, hands or joints.

11
00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:39.330
Buns use baking powder, not yeast, so there is no waiting. Mix 500 g of flour with sugar, baking powder, salt and nutmeg, then rub in 60 g of margarine until it looks like breadcrumbs.

12
00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:47.640
Add beaten eggs and milk a little at a time, until the dough is thick and sticky. It should not pour like puff-puff batter.

13
00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:58.680
Buns are thick, so use slightly cooler oil, about 160 to 170 degrees, so the inside cooks before the outside darkens.

14
00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:08.080
Drop pieces of about 40 g close to the oil surface, so they do not splash. Fry a few at a time and let the oil recover.

15
00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:20.660
Fry 6 to 8 minutes, turning, until golden, not very dark. Break one open: no wet dough inside. Afterwards, strain and store your oil, with separate oil for fish.

16
00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:30.510
Doughnuts are softer than buns, but yeast needs warmth and patience. Use lukewarm milk, never hot, because hot liquid kills yeast.

17
00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:38.900
To judge proving, press a floured finger about 1 cm into the dough. If the dent springs back quickly, it needs more time.

18
00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:55.700
If it springs back slowly and leaves a small dent, it is ready. If it does not spring back at all, it is over-proved and will soak up oil. Fry at about 170 to 175 degrees, then roll in sugar while warm.

19
00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:06.000
For example, Funke in Ibadan has an order for 45 doughnuts at 9:30 am. One batch gives about 15, so she needs 3.

20
00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:15.160
Batch A is mixed at 6:00, proved, cut, proved again, and fried from 8:00 to 8:15.

21
00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:20.100
Batch B starts 30 minutes later and fries from 8:30.

22
00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:33.090
Batch C fries from 9:00 to 9:15, 15 minutes before collection. The oil is never crowded, and she uses the gaps to clean, pack and confirm payment.

23
00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:42.190
Fish filling is moist, protein-rich food that bacteria love. Buy fresh fish, keep it cool, and use it the same day.

24
00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:47.300
Boil it until the flesh flakes easily and is opaque to the bone.

25
00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:54.840
Remove the skin and every bone. Run your fingers through it twice, because a bone is a choking hazard.

26
00:03:56.090 --> 00:04:01.770
Fry it with onion and pepper until hot and fairly dry. A wet filling makes rolls burst.

27
00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:14.130
Spread it thin to cool fast, then refrigerate. Wrap with cold filling, seal with a fork, and fry at about 165 to 175 degrees.

28
00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:19.030
Sell fish rolls the same day, labelled as containing fish, egg and wheat.

29
00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:33.870
To remember. Set up a safe frying station every time. Never use water on an oil fire. Fry in small loads. Trust the finger test. And cook fish filling fully, debone it twice and cool it fast.

30
00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:49.220
Now practise. Fry a batch of buns and record the temperature and time of each load. Make and time a doughnut batch. Then make a half batch of fish rolls, recording when the filling was cooked, cooled and refrigerated.

31
00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:51.510
Continue with the lessons below.
